Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 9 03:23:38 2026 +0000

    The compiled checker reads what a type provides by the traits chapter and checks an override's return type, reports an undeclared type in a typecase arm, and refuses a local function's untyped parameter instead of crashing

    The traits chapter says that a type does not inherit a declaration its own override declaration overrides or whose parameter types its own declaration repeats; the compiled checker read every supertype's declaration as provided and refused the team's tests/disp0.fss, which is valid by the chapter, and now reads provides as walk already did (rows 610, 617, 619, 625, 637). Under Q4's answer, way 1, a local function whose parameter type is left out gets the refusal that already stood at top level, since no text describes that inference and a stop of the checker is no answer (rows 620 to 622); the disambiguator reports an undeclared type in a typecase arm (row 626). Climb batch 11's rung C, from wip/rung-checker-overloading, with its skeptic's two fixes, one upheld by its judge; rows 650 to 653 opened.

